SPU helpers: SSE word ops, probe-free local-store access for lifted code (MAGI-6; landed on the user's order)

USER: make the fur task faster (SPU image 9, j8D485835BE6E8738, the critical
path once 0078 landed: the main thread waited ~29 ms a frame for it). Its hot
functions' instruction mix is shufb 18%, selb 15%, LS stores 12%, LS loads 7%,
then word integer ops. Two costs:

1. 27 word-wide helpers were scalar loops that clang compiles to 13-28 scalar
   instructions on 64-bit halves (spu_a, spu_ceq, spu_mpya, ...). With
   SPU_SIMD_X86 they are now one to three SSE instructions each, as 0058 did
   for the byte/halfword ones: a sf ai sfi and or xor andc nor orc andi ori
   xori ceq ceqi cgt cgti clgt clgti shli rotmi rotmai roti mpy mpya mpyu selb.
   mpy/mpya: pmaddwd of the low halfwords (the high ones masked to 0, so each
   lane is exactly the signed 16x16 product); mpyu: pmulld of the masked low
   halfwords; shifts use the SSE count semantics (>= 32 -> 0 / sign), which
   match the scalar `sh > 31` branches. The scalar versions stay as the
   #else.
2. spu_ls_read128/spu_ls_write128 paid per access for debug probes (LBP WWS
   image-2 probes, SPU_LS_LOWREAD, the LS watch list, SPU_SMC_WATCH: global
   flag loads plus a load of gpr[0] for the watch hook's arguments) and four
   scalar byte swaps. With SPU_LS_NO_PROBES (the port defines it for its
   lifted SPU sources only) each is one unaligned 16-byte load/store and one
   pshufb; the runtime's own sources keep the probe-carrying versions.

Exactness: op fuzz (each converted helper vs its scalar original, 2,000,000
inputs per op incl. 0, -1, INT_MIN/MAX, 16-bit edge values, every shift
count -128..127): 0 mismatches. Image 9 under tools/spu-opt/harness_runtime_ab.sh
(lifted image built against this tree with SPU_LS_NO_PROBES vs the old tree,
every function on the same random gpr + LS state, all gprs, LS and the rest
of the context compared): 743 identical, the 23 loop functions run with their
counters seeded identical, 4 not testable in the harness (stubs / no counter).
A/B (drive_gameplay, simultaneous, same tree otherwise): mg6-op1 29.74 vs
mg6-op0 23.95 flips/s (+24%); 0 FATAL, 0 LIFT-GAP.

